claim.claim-text:
a superior portion of the contact lens;
an inferior portion of the contact lens;
a lens portion; and
a portion for lid attachment located in the superior portion of the contact lens, the portion for lid attachment having a thickness greater than a thickness of the lens at its center, wherein the contact lens attaches to an upper eyelid of a wearer by the portion for lid attachment interacting with an upper tarsal plate of the upper eyelid of a wearer, said interaction allows the contact lens to translate upwards in downgaze, and
wherein the portion for lid attachment has a top surface, said top surface having a shape selected from the group consisting of flat, flat with rounded corners, concave, convex or tapered having a thicker portion closer to an edge of the contact lens, or combinations thereof.

a superior portion of the contact lens;
an inferior portion of the contact lens;
a lens portion; and
a portion for lid attachment located in the superior portion of the contact lens, the portion for lid attachment having a thickness greater than a thickness of the lens at its center, wherein the contact lens attaches to an upper eyelid of a wearer by the portion for lid attachment interacting with an upper tarsal plate of the upper eyelid of a wearer, said interaction allows the contact lens to translate upwards in downgaze, and
wherein the portion for lid attachment is comprised of a plurality of sections, each section thicker than the thickness at the central portion of the contact lens.

a superior portion of the contact lens;
an inferior portion of the contact lens;
a lens portion; and
a portion for lid attachment located in the superior portion of the contact lens, the portion for lid attachment having a thickness greater than a thickness of the lens at its center, wherein the contact lens attaches to an upper eyelid of a wearer by the portion for lid attachment interacting with an upper tarsal plate of the upper eyelid of a wearer, said interaction allows the contact lens to translate upwards in downgaze, and
wherein the portion for lid attachment interacts with an upper tarsal plate of an upper eyelid of the wearer and said portion for lid attachment is configured to attach the contact lens to the upper eyelid, said attachment translating the contact lens upwards in a downgaze of the wearer, and
wherein the portion for lid attachment has an anatomical shape.
